From 8524e586f856a54623a35695e94ea2aa28b7a265 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Egor 835 <egor.su.8@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:27:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64: configs: msm8953-perf: Default to CUBIC congestion
 control

BBR relies on pacing, and without the fq qdisc (not enabled here) TCP
falls back to internal pacing with a per-socket hrtimer. On this 4.19
kernel tcp_pace_kick() storms: a trace during a Telegram upload over
OpenVPN showed ~290k tcp_pace_kick expiries per second, the HRTIMER
softirq ate 1-2.5 CPUs at 1-4 Mbit/s and the whole UI stuttered. With
cubic the same upload runs at 13-20 Mbit/s with 5-9% softirq time.
Keep BBR built in for anyone selecting it explicitly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/vendor/msm8953-perf_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/msm8953-perf_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/msm8953-perf_defconfig
index 80b8b917d..126a2087e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/msm8953-perf_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/msm8953-perf_defconfig
@@ -749,7 +749,7 @@ CONFIG_TCP_CONG_BIC=y
 CONFIG_TCP_CONG_WESTWOOD=y
 CONFIG_TCP_CONG_HTCP=y
 CONFIG_TCP_CONG_BBR=y
-CONFIG_DEFAULT_BBR=y
+CONFIG_DEFAULT_CUBIC=y
 
 # USB
 CONFIG_USB=y
-- 
2.56.0

